From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fsck_hfs: copy a complete fixed-size dummy volume name

Use a zero-initialized Str27 object rather than reading sizeof(Str27) bytes
from a shorter string literal. Preserve the Pascal length byte and name.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/fsck_hfs.tproj/dfalib/SVerify1.c
+++ b/fsck_hfs.tproj/dfalib/SVerify1.c
@@ -3454,7 +3454,8 @@ OSErr	VLockedChk( SGlobPtr GPtr )
 	}
 	else		//	Because we don't have the unicode converters, just fill it with a dummy name.
 	{
-		CopyMemory( "\x0dPure HFS Plus", calculatedVCB->vcbVN, sizeof(Str27) );
+		static const Str27 dummyName = "\x0dPure HFS Plus";
+		CopyMemory( dummyName, calculatedVCB->vcbVN, sizeof(dummyName) );
 	}
 		
 	GPtr->TarBlock = hint;
